  "answer":"No. The current release policy does not allow accuracy > 0.80 alone to authorize a production release. According to the release‑policy, a model may be promoted only if it shows an improvement of at least 0.005 in F1 on a frozen holdout and its ROC‑AUC does not drop by more than 0.01. The legacy memo that permitted releases based solely on accuracy > 0.80 is explicitly superseded by this release‑policy, so the old rule no longer applies.",
